module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Size.Coverings
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fppf

/-!
# From a covering sieve of a big fppf site to a covering family

The sheaf condition, and every statement derived from it, hands out covering *sieves*: the
sheafification machinery of `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.imageSieve_mem` produces a member of
`GrothendieckTopology`, and the topology of a big fppf site is generated from its chosen
covering families rather than equal to them.  A covering sieve is closed under precomposition,
so it contains composites `g ≫ f` which are not themselves flat or of finite presentation.  Any
argument that reasons from a property of the covering *morphisms* — flatness, openness, finite
presentation, affineness — therefore has to descend from the sieve to a family first.

This file performs that descent, for a big fppf site and for its slice over a scheme `S`.  The
work is done once and generically: a sieve covering for the topology generated by a system of
covering families satisfying the site axioms contains the sieve generated by one of those
families.  The three site axioms are used exactly once each, in the three inductive steps of
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.Saturate` beyond the generating one: isomorphisms for the top sieve,
base change for pullback stability, and composition for the local character axiom.

The slice case is not the generated topology of a precoverage on the slice but Mathlib's
localized topology `B.topology.over (B.obj hS)`, so it is reduced to the case of the ambient
site through `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff` and the resulting family is
lifted back into the slice.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.fppfCovering`: the family of scheme morphisms underlying a
  chosen covering family, as an `AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering`.  This is what makes
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering.isOpenMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering.exists_finite_affineOpens_cover` available to an argument that
  started from a covering sieve.

## Main results

* `exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le`: generically, a covering sieve of the topology generated by the
  covering families of a site contains the sieve of a covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le`: the same for a big fppf site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.jointlySurjective_and_flat_and_lfp_of_isCovering`: the
  morphisms of a chosen covering family are jointly surjective, flat and locally of finite
  presentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le`: the same descent for the big fppf
  site of a scheme `S`, where the topology is the localized one.

## Implementation notes

The generic statement takes the presenting precoverage as a variable together with the
hypothesis that its covering presieves are exactly those generated by the chosen families,
which holds by `Iff.rfl` for `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.precoverage`.  Stating it that way
keeps the lemma applicable to the other big sites of the library, whose precoverages are built
to the same pattern.

This route needs none of the four `CategoryTheory.Precoverage` stability classes that
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition` asks for: the
three site axioms recorded in `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.coverings_isSite` are used
directly, and they are stated for the *bounded* system, so the family produced here satisfies
the site's cardinality bound as well as being fppf.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 021R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 021S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021S)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe uC vC u

/-- A family generates a subsieve of `S` as soon as each of its members lies in `S`. -/
private theorem sieve₀_le_of_forall_mem {C : Type*} [Category C] {X : C}
    {E : PreZeroHypercover X} {S : Sieve X} (h : ∀ i, S (E.f i)) : E.sieve₀ ≤ S := by
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff, Presieve.ofArrows_le_iff]
  exact h

/-- **A covering sieve contains a covering family.**  Let `IsCov` be a system of covering
families satisfying the site axioms and let `J` be the precoverage whose covering presieves are
those generated by the members of `IsCov`.  Then every sieve covering for the Grothendieck
topology generated by `J` contains the sieve generated by some family in `IsCov`.

This is what lets an argument about a big site use flatness, finite presentation or openness of
the covering morphisms: those are properties of a family, and the sheaf condition supplies only
a sieve. -/
public theorem exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le
    {C : Type uC} [Category.{vC} C] {IsCov : Covering.{uC, vC, max uC vC} C → Prop}
    (hsite : IsSite IsCov) {J : Precoverage C}
    (hJ : ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X), R ∈ J X ↔
      ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{max uC vC} X, R = E.presieve₀ ∧ IsCov ⟨X, E⟩)
    {X : C} {S : Sieve X} (hS : S ∈ J.toGrothendieck X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{max uC vC} X, IsCov ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ E.sieve₀ ≤ S := by
  rw [Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff] at hS
  induction hS with
  | of X R hR =>
      obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := (hJ _ _).mp hR
      exact ⟨E, hE, le_rfl⟩
  | top X =>
      refine ⟨PreZeroHypercover.singleton (𝟙 X), hsite.1 (𝟙 X), ?_⟩
      simp
  | pullback X S hS Y f ih =>
      obtain ⟨E, hE, hES⟩ := ih
      obtain ⟨P, π₁, π₂, hpull, hP⟩ := hsite.2.2 ⟨X, E⟩ hE Y f
      refine ⟨⟨E.I₀, P, π₂⟩, hP, sieve₀_le_of_forall_mem fun i => ?_⟩
      have hmem : S (π₁ i ≫ E.f i) := S.downward_closed (hES _ (E.sieve₀_f i)) (π₁ i)
      change S (π₂ i ≫ f)
      rwa [(hpull i).w] at hmem
  | transitive X S R hS hlocal ihS ihlocal =>
      obtain ⟨E, hE, hES⟩ := ihS
      have hloc (i : E.I₀) :
          ∃ F : PreZeroHypercover (E.X i),
            IsCov ⟨E.X i, F⟩ ∧ F.sieve₀ ≤ R.pullback (E.f i) :=
        ihlocal (hES _ (E.sieve₀_f i))
      choose F hF hFR using hloc
      refine ⟨E.bind F, ?_, ?_⟩
      · simpa [PreZeroHypercover.pushforward] using hsite.2.1 ⟨X, E⟩ hE
          (fun i => ⟨E.X i, F i⟩) hF (fun _ => rfl)
      · exact sieve₀_le_of_forall_mem fun ⟨i, j⟩ => hFR i _ ((F i).sieve₀_f j)

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **A covering sieve of a big fppf site contains a chosen covering family.**  The chosen
families satisfy the site axioms by `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.coverings_isSite`, and the
topology is generated by them. -/
public theorem BigFppfSite.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes}
    {S : Sieve X} (hS : S ∈ B.topology X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X, B.IsCovering ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ E.sieve₀ ≤ S :=
  _root_.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le B.isSite (fun _ _ => Iff.rfl) hS

/-- The morphisms of a chosen covering family of a big fppf site are jointly surjective, flat
and locally of finite presentation: that is what membership in the fppf precoverage of all
schemes, comapped along the site's inclusion, says. -/
public theorem BigFppfSite.jointlySurjective_and_flat_and_lfp_of_isCovering
    (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes} {E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X}
    (hE : B.IsCovering ⟨X, E⟩) :
    (∀ x, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (B.inclusion.map (E.f i))) ∧
      ∀ i, Flat (B.inclusion.map (E.f i)) ∧
        LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map (E.f i)) := by
  have h : E.presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage.comap B.inclusion X :=
    B.isFppfCovering_of_isCovering hE
  rwa [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map,
    show Scheme.fppfPrecoverage =
      Scheme.precoverage (@Flat ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) from rfl,
    Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff] at h

/-- **The covering family underlying a chosen covering family of a big fppf site.**  Its
morphisms are flat, locally of finite presentation and jointly surjective, so the openness and
quasi-compactness machinery of `AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering` applies to it — in particular
`AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering.isOpenMap` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FppfCovering.exists_finite_affineOpens_cover`. -/
public def BigFppfSite.fppfCovering (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes}
    {E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X} (hE : B.IsCovering ⟨X, E⟩) :
    FppfCovering.{u + 1} (B.inclusion.obj X) where
  ι := E.I₀
  X i := B.inclusion.obj (E.X i)
  f i := B.inclusion.map (E.f i)
  flat i := (B.jointlySurjective_and_flat_and_lfp_of_isCovering hE).2 i |>.1
  lfp i := (B.jointlySurjective_and_flat_and_lfp_of_isCovering hE).2 i |>.2
  jointly_surjective t := (B.jointlySurjective_and_flat_and_lfp_of_isCovering hE).1 t

/-- **A covering sieve of the big fppf site of `S` contains a chosen covering family.**  The
topology of the slice is the localized topology, so a covering sieve on an object `X ⟶ S`
corresponds to a covering sieve on `X` in the ambient site; the family obtained there is lifted
back into the slice by composing its members with the structure morphism of `X`. -/
public theorem BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) {X : BigFppfOver B S hS} {T : Sieve X}
    (hT : T ∈ BigFppfOver.topology B S hS X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X, BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ E.sieve₀ ≤ T := by
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hT
  obtain ⟨E₀, hE₀, hle⟩ := B.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le hT
  exact ⟨⟨E₀.I₀, fun i => Over.mk (E₀.f i ≫ X.hom), fun i => Over.homMk (E₀.f i) (by simp)⟩,
    hE₀, sieve₀_le_of_forall_mem fun i =>
      (Sieve.overEquiv_iff T (E₀.f i)).mp (hle _ (E₀.sieve₀_f i))⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
